// REQUIRES: host-linux-amd64 || host-linux-arm64
// RUN: not %gopp build -emit=gir %S/Inputs/recursive-no-struct.gopp 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %gopp build %gopp_link_flags %S/Inputs/recursive-through-struct.gopp -o %t.ok
// RUN: %t.ok | FileCheck --check-prefix=OK %s
// P04.04 (review R14): a defined type that reaches itself through Option, a
// pointer or an array but no struct has no GIR type that can name itself (the
// struct is the one nominal type). It is refused with one E0439 per type that
// names it, never a null without a report (which dropped `f` silently or
// crashed in a later step), and nothing else is reported for it. Both sides:
// the cycles through a struct (a list, a tree with Options) lower and run.
// CHECK: recursive-no-struct.gopp:9:1: error[E0439]: the type *main.L, which refers to itself through no struct (P04.05), is not supported
// CHECK: recursive-no-struct.gopp:12:6: error[E0439]: the type main.A, which refers to itself through no struct (P04.05), is not supported
// CHECK: recursive-no-struct.gopp:13:6: error[E0439]: the type main.O, which refers to itself through no struct (P04.05), is not supported
// CHECK-NOT: error
// OK: 2 false true 0 2
